#Problem Statement

Despite having millions of tracks, Spotify’s discovery experience heavily favors popular artists and algorithmic playlists.
Independent and emerging artists struggle to gain visibility, limiting their ability to build an audience organically.

Additionally, Spotify does not allow users to download individual songs directly neither in paid nor in unpaid version.
Users must add songs to playlists or albums, which creates friction and  reduces low-commitment sampling and results in fewer saves,
follows, and repeat listens for independent creators.

This results in fewer meaningful discovery opportunities for indie artists and limited exploration behavior from listeners.
